From 3c888208b723200b86fc77b6341cfd4cfc2e1076 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luannt <luannt.devops@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:42:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent,backend): record a prompt durably before
 acknowledging it

`send` without --wait returned 0 before the user message was written, and
queued prompts lived only in memory: killing or stopping the server lost them
with no trace (7-8/8 kills lost the prompt; a queued prompt vanished on
SIGTERM). SendMessage now writes the user message plus a pending reply
placeholder in one transaction before it acks. The turn takes the pair over;
dropped prompts (Esc, ClearQueue, Ctrl+C on `run`) close the placeholder as
canceled, a failure before any reply closes it with the real error, and after a
crash the existing settle step shows Interrupted. Nothing reruns on its own.

The placeholder points to its user message by ID, so prompts that have not run
yet (or were dropped) stay out of every model request regardless of row order,
including under concurrent sends; the model never sees a canceled prompt, as in
V2. Multi-row writes (pair, move, reply+placeholder delete) go through
message.WriteBatch, so a crash cannot leave two copies. Settle does not touch
live placeholders, queue DB writes happen outside the dispatch lock, stats and
`run --json` skip placeholders, and the provider ID agent-cli-pending is
reserved. Client/server mode only; in-process mode is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
